00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.540
I think people have to break patterns.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.280
I think you do something different

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:56.500
or build courage to do something different

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.620
by getting used to it.

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.735
The great fortune of my
life was I was an immigrant

00:21:59.735 --> 00:22:03.030
who got picked on for not
being able to speak English.

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:06.013
I was a terrible student,
I was not good at sports.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:08.990
I basically lived the
first 18 years of my life

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:11.260
telling me that I was a losing player.

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.810
So I got real cozy with losing.

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.650
I loved losing, it's why I associate

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:20.130
so much more with people that
don't come from privilege.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:21.607
Whether they look that part and look,

00:22:21.607 --> 00:22:24.023
I view privilege first and foremost,

00:22:24.023 --> 00:22:27.930
we don't have, we can see a
white male looks privileged.

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:31.040
We can see somebody who's well
off financially as privilege.

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:32.900
The real privilege game in our society

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:35.150
is what's going on in everybody's dome.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:37.263
Mental privilege is number one.

00:22:42.322 --> 00:22:44.570
This is why I talk so
much about parenting.

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:47.670
We're living through the worst execution

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:49.430
of parenting in our society

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:54.040
because we're living through
such enormous success,

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:59.040
abundance and prosperity in
America for the last 67 years

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:01.460
and so now parents are
getting into things.

00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:04.120
You know, parents during
the great depression

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:07.930
struggled with going to school
and yelling at the teacher

00:23:07.930 --> 00:23:10.140
for not doing this,
that or the other thing.

00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:12.880
So we're living in eighth place trophies,

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:14.700
fake environments, entitlement.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.930
There are kids in this room right now

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:19.370
who take money from their parents

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.310
and are over the age of 22.

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:24.830
I believe that that is the
number one poison in our society.

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:27.540
I believe it creates
enormous fake environments.

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:29.800
It subconsciously tells children

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.410
that they're not capable and
they need their parents help

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.470
and fake environments are bad

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:36.223
and it leads to bad behavior.

00:23:38.029 --> 00:23:38.920
Do you know that our society

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.870
doesn't talk about saving money at all?

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:44.210
We don't talk about saving money at all.

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:46.370
We don't talk about borrowing
money from our parents

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:48.210
and paying them back, that's what

00:23:48.210 --> 00:23:49.840
two generations ago used to do.

00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:53.733
Now we just, we're so fucking
entitled, we just expect.

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:56.347
Everybody always asks me,

00:23:56.347 --> 00:24:00.470
"Hey, how do I manage these millennials?"

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:02.030
I'm like, "With empathy."

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:03.410
they were parented in an environment

00:24:03.410 --> 00:24:06.206
where if you came in ninth,
they clapped for you.

00:24:06.206 --> 00:24:09.039
(audience laughs)

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:14.350
listen, I think this is a
super important subject matter.

00:24:14.350 --> 00:24:16.604
I'm not saying boo somebody
and make them feel like,

00:24:16.604 --> 00:24:19.140
I'm a product of self-esteem.

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:21.050
My Mom did the greatest job of self-esteem

00:24:21.050 --> 00:24:23.133
but she also created accountability.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.180
And we really need to debate that.

00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:29.910
